 scoped only 'for CHANGELOG mirroring.' AC2's grep excludes docs, so no test catches the resulting stale narrative.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f85da010b64a404bf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope ('Out of scope: ... the historical docs/release-notes.md:696-698'); Approach > CHANGELOG ('Mirror in docs/release-notes.md')","norm_id":"n2fa4b451983aedc4","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After implementation, release-notes.md:1411-1413 still describes a removed github-api source as retained; readers believe the rollback knob exists","A future grep over docs (unlike AC2's scripts/.github/tests scope) finds the stale reference"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Enumerate docs/release-notes.md:1405-1414 as a consumer to update (rewrite to drop the retained `github-api` rollback source), and fix the Out-of-scope line to cite the actually-historical canary reference (or remove the 696-698 citation, which is unrelated signing content).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the detect_config.py rationale: the mechanism ratchet consumes gen_env_registry.scan() + _derived_env_names(), not render(), so a render()-only change adds no env_var:: entries at all; restate the asymmetry note (detect_config.py:8-15, architecture.md:669) in terms of the scan()/render() boundary rather than 'no marker path for dozens of new entries'.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["detect_config.py:88 `reads, _dynamic = registry.scan(repo_root / \"src\" / \"rebar\")` — the ratchet reads scan(), not render()","Plan scopes the change to render(): 'In render() replace the MCP_ENV_VARS-only union (:406-409) with a loop over _SECTIONS'","render() and scan() are separate functions (scan at gen_env_registry.py:349); derived names added only in render() never reach _derived_env_names() or detect_env_vars()"],"finding":"The Approach's rationale for leaving scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py:63-81 untouched rests on an inaccurate data-flow claim: it says the render() change would add 'dozens of new env_var:: entries' tripping check_mechanism_delta. But detect_env_vars (detect_config.py:83-97) consumes registry.scan()+_derived_env_names(), not render(); a render()-only edit adds zero entries to the ratchet census. The conclusion (don't touch the detector) is correct, but the stated reason is wrong and the docstring/architecture 'asymmetry' note built on it would memorialize an incorrect mechanism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffa03bce6588c5435","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Registry bullet ('Do not change scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py:63-81 — dozens of new env_var:: entries would trip check_mechanism_delta')","norm_id":"n091c0ef52154d2d0","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer, trusting the stated premise, adds the derived names into scan() (believing render() alone is what the ratchet sees) and actually trips check_mechanism_delta --check — the exact failure the plan wanted to avoid","The architecture.md:669 'deliberate asymmetry' note gets written to describe a ratchet behavior that does not occur, confusing future readers"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the derived names are added in render() (the doc generator) only, and that detect_env_vars() reads scan(), whose 'actually-read under src/rebar' semantics are intentionally unchanged — so the ratchet census is unaffected because the new names never enter scan()/_derived_env_names(), and a derived name's definition site (its _SECTIONS row) is already censused as config_key/feature_flag.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify keeping the env-registry derivation and the canary `github-api` retirement in one ticket, or split them into separate children — they are disjoint in files, concern, and acceptance proof, with only the CHANGELOG bookkeeping loosely coupling them.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["G5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1286,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Title: 'Derive every canonical env name in the env registry, retire the canary github-api source, and file the CHANGELOG bookkeeping' — three goals joined by 'and'","AC1 touches only `scripts/gen_env_registry.py`, `docs/env-vars.md`, `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`; AC2 touches only `canary_bridge.py`, the workflow, ADR 0094, and canary tests — disjoint file sets","The CHANGELOG bookkeeping is the only thread loosely tying them (it documents both), but the registry and canary deliverables share no code and no test"],"finding":"The ticket bundles three independently-releasable outcomes joined by a structural 'and' in the title: (1) deriving every canonical env name into the registry, (2) retiring the canary `github-api` heartbeat source, and (3) CHANGELOG/release-notes bookkeeping. The registry derivation (AC1, `gen_env_registry.py`/`docs/env-vars.md`) and the canary retirement (AC2, `canary_bridge.py`/workflow/ADR 0094) are disjoint in files, personas (doc-completeness vs ADR-driven CI cleanup), and acceptance proofs — each is independently valuable, testable, and releasable; neither is order-dependent on the other.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdedff229c0b8231a","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Title / Scope / Acceptance Criteria (AC1 vs AC2)","norm_id":"n2748cf105fd9d4f6","priority":0.4714,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"If these are siblings under one epic (as the Context implies with 'upstream siblings'), consider filing the registry-derivation and canary-retirement as separate children, each carrying its own CHANGELOG/release-notes bullet, rather than one combined ticket.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_